# Claude settings sync rules
# Scopes the source that propagates the [claude] grove.toml profile
# (permissions.allow + sandbox{enabled, failIfUnavailable,
# autoAllowBashIfSandboxed, filesystem.allowWrite, network.allowedDomains}) into
# each workspace/worktree's .claude/settings.local.json: the leaf config struct
# + seeder, the per-worktree member-repo union resolver, the worktree-creation
# call sites, the local daemon watcher, and the manual grove-anthropic
# sync-settings command. Changes to any of these should trigger the
# claude-settings-sync E2E scenario, which drives a real `sync-settings --all`
# across an ecosystem and asserts the merged/unioned/no-clobber result.
# Paths are relative to the flow repo root.

../core/pkg/claudenotebook/config.go
../core/pkg/claudenotebook/seeder.go
../core/pkg/workspace/claude_notebook.go
../core/pkg/workspace/prepare.go
cmd/plan_add_worktrees.go
../daemon/internal/daemon/watcher/claude_settings.go
../grove-anthropic/cmd/sync_settings.go
tests/e2e/tend/scenarios/claude_settings_sync.go
